{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Correction to the previous comment: the sentence \"re-running the 7 implicated FP cases once each produced 0 findings on all 7\" is not supported. Those runs failed before reaching the model — the Bedrock backend had no AWS profile selected, so each `run_case` raised, and the harness recorded the error as a case with zero findings. Zero findings there means the call never happened, not that the reviewer stayed quiet.\n\nRe-running the same diagnostic with `AWS_PROFILE=frontier` set, which is what the full eval runs had. Everything else in the previous comment stands: the baseline and e508 eval runs both scored normally (coverage 1.0, 2028s and 2626s), so their per-epoch failure counts are real measurements.\n\nThe per-case false-fire rate of roughly 0.17 therefore rests on the two full eval runs alone, and the claim that the over-firing is intermittent rather than a deterministic wrong guard is currently unsupported. The re-run decides it: repeated fires on the same case point at a specific guard to fix, scattered fires point at calibration."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793815697992470470,"uuid":"b80d1164-880a-4657-9228-5d6cca285efe"}